Description: SecuBox LED heartbeat status indicator
 Visual system health indicator using MOCHAbin RGB LEDs.
 .
 Displays system health, security status, and resource usage
 via the IS31FL3199 I2C LED controller (3 RGB LEDs).
 .
 The leds-is31fl319x driver, missing from the Debian stock kernel, is built
 by DKMS on MOCHAbin only. dkms and linux-headers-arm64 are only suggested
 (installed by the MOCHAbin provisioning or by hand), so other boards and a
 MOCHAbin without I2C bus pull no kernel headers.
 .
 Display engine (secubox-led-pulse): ordered layers from
 /etc/secubox/leds.toml, by default eight sequences of 8 s: system (CPU,
 memory, I/O), network, firewall, WAF, Actor, AdGuard, services and SOC,
 coloured green/cyan/yellow/orange/red from levels computed by the
 secubox-led-flux collector against a per-box adaptive reference (violet
 while learning). Shapes: par_led, jauge, mono, double, triple, etale,
 rotatif. Writes only changed channels, rate-bounded (20 writes/s by
 default).
